<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A function whose definite integral is zero</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Give a polynomial \(f(x)\) of degree at most \(3\) with \(f(0) = {@v0@}\) and \(\displaystyle \int_0^{ {@hh@} } f(x)\,dx = 0\).</p><div>\(f(x) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Which statement is true for every correct answer to (a)?</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) Many answers are possible. Try \(f(x) = {@v0@} + ax\): then \(f(0) = {@v0@}\) and \(\displaystyle \int_0^{ {@hh@} } ({@v0@} + ax)\,dx = {@v0*hh@} + {@hh^2/2@}a\). This is \(0\) when \(a = {@-2*v0/hh@}\), giving \(f(x) = {@samp@}\). Another answer is \(f(x) = {@alt@}\).</p><p>(b) If the graph stayed on one side of the \(x\)-axis, every strip would have the same sign and the integral could not be \(0\). So the graph must cross the axis between \(x = 0\) and \(x = {@hh@}\): the area above the axis cancels the area below in the integral. The area itself is not \(0\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_poly3(ex) := if not every(lambda([v], member(v, [x])), listofvars(ex)) then "Use x as the variable." else if not polynomialp(ev(expand(ex), simp), [x]) then "Enter a polynomial in x, for example 3-2x." else if hipow(ev(expand(ex), simp), x) > 3 then "Keep to degree 3 or less." else "";
/* Design: construct-an-example pattern. [h, v0, position of "cross" (2 or 3, never first)]. Source: original. */
L: [[2,3,2],[3,-2,3],[4,5,2],[1,4,3],[6,-3,2],[2,-5,3],[3,6,2],[4,-1,3],[1,-4,2],[6,2,3]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
hh: L[ix][1]; v0: L[ix][2]; pos: L[ix][3];
samp: v0-2*v0*x/hh;
oside: ["side", false, sconcat("The graph of \\(y = f(x)\\) stays on one side of the \\(x\\)-axis for \\(0 \\le x \\le ", hh, "\\).")];
ocross: ["cross", true, sconcat("The graph of \\(y = f(x)\\) crosses the \\(x\\)-axis somewhere between \\(x = 0\\) and \\(x = ", hh, "\\).")];
ozero: ["zero", false, sconcat("The area between the graph and the \\(x\\)-axis from \\(x = 0\\) to \\(x = ", hh, "\\) is \\(0\\).")];
opts: if pos=2 then [oside, ocross, ozero] else [ozero, oside, ocross];
alt: v0-4*v0/hh^3*x^3;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
